>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_bflag`

``` hol4
HOLFlags.set_bflag : bflag * bool -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Set a boolean flag.

A call to `set_bflag (f, b)` sets the flag `f` to `b`, for the rest of
the session or until something sets it again. To set one only for the
duration of a call, use `with_bflags`.

The flag is a value rather than a name, so a misspelling is a compile
error rather than a failure when the line is reached; `set_trace` is the
equivalent that takes the trace's name as a string.

### Failure

Fails if `f` does not name a trace, which can happen only if the flag
was built by hand rather than obtained from `create_btrace`.

### Example

``` hol4
>> HOLFlags.set_bflag (Parse.show_types, true);

>> ``$=``;

>>__ HOLFlags.set_bflag (Parse.show_types, false);
```

